    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1303">

                <pb facs="1119" n="1015" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1015"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 881.111/1</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Chargé d’Affaires.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-03-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 26, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your 370, March 4. Clause referred to would seem sufficient if changed to read as
                    follows: “the Diplomatic Body reserves to its respective Governments”. Always
                    bearing in mind the insistence of this Government that its treaty rights shall
                    continue to be recognized, you will so far as possible act in accord with your
                    colleagues.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Adee</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
